# Point Commitment — "I know a G1 point P such that H(P) == y"
#
# Proves knowledge of a secret G1 curve point whose MiMC hash matches a
# public commitment. Useful for committing to a curve point (e.g. a public
# key or shared secret) and revealing it only on demand.
#
# This is the curve-point analogue of simple-preimage.pattern: same
# commit-reveal pattern, but the secret is a G1 point instead of a scalar.
#
# How H(G1) works in-circuit (handled automatically by Claude):
#   - The Fp coordinates X, Y are each reduced to a single native Fr element
#     via limb arithmetic: x_fr = Σ limb[i] * (2^(64*i) mod r).
#   - Both Fr elements are fed to MiMC, which produces a single Fr digest.
#   - The off-chain prover mirrors this exactly: bls12381_fr.Element.SetBigInt
#     auto-reduces mod r, so writing those marshaled bytes to native MiMC
#     produces the same digest.
#
# This demonstrates: Secret G1 input, hashing a curve point with MiMC.

Secret G1 Inputs: (p)
Public Int Inputs: (y)

compute: h = H(p)
check: y == h
